      "writtenOn": "2019-02-28T00:54:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is always needed if the charge_manager_source_port previously set CONFIG_USB_PD_MAX_SINGLE_SOURCE_CURRENT on the port.  If the charge_manager_source_port set CONFIG_USB_PD_PULLUP, this call doesn\u0027t cost us much time since it only caches the value.\n\nThis addition is necessary to avoid triggering CCD on dongles with Rd/Ra.  Presenting 3A in that scenario can cause CCD mode detection until the set_state line 738 tcpm_select_rp_value() code runs (on our systems, for about 30 ms, which is long enough to kill display communication for some HDMI dongles)",
      "parentUuid": "3aa6a06e_db1e5f0b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4132,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 4133,
        "endChar": 33
